a9e-1b74509a4df1" :question/math-academy-id "q-99263" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨1,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨1,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨1,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int 1\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-99263/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-99263"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-99392/selection/95bf8c5d972d9acd3b011bd97a0305b2020dc3e7fa602db33ae3622f468bb18a" :answer/id #uuid "d55e86e8-b5aa-5e1a-84bd-7703bb7915ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{3}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3},\\,-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99392/selection/d7f0049cf3d32666d621a973b97205c725d82ef1bb931035e703a5a3065844c3" :answer/id #uuid "84ac24b3-f933-53cf-a0d6-ddd5c3822cc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{3}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3},\\,-\\operatorname{csc}⁡t⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99392/selection/ac8b72dd7277e4f307dbdf99daaaef2de122d9ed81d6d1750d4e69e88f477914" :answer/id #uuid "7a773244-de03-5f03-aa3d-8a49dab4c5b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\,-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t⟩+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99392/selection/d39ed6c4a1cbb811842bb4164eb98e4f04fe5a213c